<title>UK: HSBC buys Polish brokerage firm.</title>
<headline>HSBC buys Polish brokerage firm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>HSBC Investment Banking said on Monday it had bought brokerage firm Dom Inwestycyjny Guziejewski i Albrecht SA in Lodz, Poland.</p>
<p>The company, part of HSBC Holdings Plc, said its offer was accepted by shareholders holding 98.57 percent of the firm's shares.</p>
<p>The firm had a net asset value of about 300,000 stg, HSBC said in a statement.</p>
<p>Other financial terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
